{"body":"**MUST-FIX**: This relative import is not valid in the built daemon layout. `build:daemon` copies this file to `dist/daemon/shadow-sync.ts`, so `../../parser/shadow.js` resolves to `parser/shadow.js` at repo root instead of `dist/parser/shadow.js`. That makes daemon startup fail on the packaged/runtime path, which matches the red smoke CI.","id":2901701222,"line":null,"path":"packages/daemon/src/shadow-sync.ts"}
{"body":"**MUST-FIX**: Same runtime path problem here. From `dist/daemon/server.ts`, `../../parser/config.js` resolves outside `dist`, so the daemon cannot load project config during startup. The current PR head already shows this as `e2e (playwright smoke)` failing with `Daemon failed to start within 5 seconds`.","id":2901701224,"line":null,"path":"packages/daemon/src/server.ts"}
{"body":"**MUST-FIX**: This PR covers write-side sync, but the task description also requires pulling fresh shadow state before CLI read operations such as `task list` and similar read paths. Those code paths are unchanged in this branch, so a second clone can still read stale task/spec state until manual `kspec shadow sync` or the daemon interval happens to run.","id":2901902216,"line":1441,"path":"src/parser/shadow.ts"}
{"body":"**MUST-FIX**: This pre-read sync path drops the resolved shadow config. `hasRemoteTracking(specDir)` and `shadowPull(specDir)` fall back to `kspec-meta`/`origin`, so custom `shadow.branch` or `shadow.remote` setups silently skip sync or use the wrong upstream. Pass the resolved shadow options through here.","id":2901926252,"line":395,"path":"src/parser/yaml.ts"}
{"body":"**MUST-FIX**: This file copies `ShadowSyncScheduler` instead of importing the production class, so `@config-shadow ac-12` is not actually covered on the shipped daemon code path. A regression in `packages/daemon/src/shadow-sync.ts` could pass this suite unchanged.","id":2901926254,"line":21,"path":"tests/shadow-sync-scheduler.test.ts"}
{"body":"**MUST-FIX**: `remoteBranchExists(projectRoot, branchName)` still defaults to `origin`. That breaks the new bidirectional sync flow for configured remotes (`shadow.remote` named/path/url), which is already part of `@config-shadow`. This lookup needs to follow the branch's configured upstream, not hardcode the default.","id":2901926615,"line":1330,"path":"src/parser/shadow.ts"}

